    "result": "Perfect! The fix is complete and working correctly. \n\n## Summary\n\nI fixed the bug where `frai gate init --ci` wasn't creating the GitHub Actions workflow file. The issue was in the `frai` CLI's command setup in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`.\n\n**The Problem:** \nThe `--ci` flag was defined on the main program, so Commander.js's parser was consuming it at the parent level before the `gate` subcommand could receive it.\n\n**The Solution:**\nAdded `.passThroughOptions()` to the main program (line 604) to tell Commander.js to pass options through to subcommands instead of consuming them at the parent level.\n\n**Changes Made:**\n- Modified `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` line 604 to add `.passThroughOptions()`\n- Rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n\n**Verification:**\n\u2705 `FRAI-SPEC.md` is created  \n\u2705 `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` is now created with the correct GitHub Actions configuration",
